摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DeepSeek Harness plugin: answer the built-in web_search with your own RustXNG metasearch instance (Windows / macOS / Linux)","id":"gh:1433086065","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-rustxng","slug":"kgmkm/dsh-rustxng","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","metasearch","rustxng","searxng"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness plugin: answer the built-in web_search with your own RustXNG metasearch instance (W"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"indows / macOS / Linux)"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-rustxng"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Use a self-hosted RustXNG instance from\nDeepSeek Harness — and answer the\nbuilt-in **`web_search`** "},{"id":"p3s2","text":"lf-hosted RustXNG instance from\nDeepSeek Harness — and answer the\nbuilt-in **`web_search`** with it."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"RustXNG is a SearXNG-compatible metasearch engine written in Rust: one query fans out to\nover a hund"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"red search engines (119 enabled in 0.28's default `standard` profile),\ndeduplicates the results and "},{"id":"p4s3","text":"returns them without ads or tracking. This\nplugin connects DSH to a RustXNG you run yourself (Window"},{"id":"p4s4","text":"s, macOS or Linux)\nand adds:"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"| Contribution | What it gives you |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Search provider** | A `rustxng` provider on"},{"id":"p5s2","text":" the web seam. Point `web.searchProvider` at it and the built-in `web_search` is answered by your in"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"stance — no DeepSeek search API key involved. |\n| **Settings card** | A card in **Plugins** with two"},{"id":"p5s4","text":" live switches and the instance URL. No restart, no hand-edited YAML. |\n| **Tools** | `rustxng_searc"},{"id":"p5s5","text":"h` (engine, category, language and time-range scoped) and `rustxng_status` (reachability, version, e"},{"id":"p5s6","text":"ngine count, provider state). |\n| **Fetch provider** (optional) | A charset-aware `web_fetch`: resol"},{"id":"p5s7","text":"ves BOM → HTTP header → `<meta charset>` before decoding, so Shift_JIS pages that declare their enco"},{"id":"p5s8","text":"ding only in `<meta>` stop coming back as `�`. Does not use RustXNG. |\n| **Process supervision** (op"},{"id":"p5s9","text":"tional) | Start the binary when the instance does not answer, and stop it again after an idle timeou"},{"id":"p5s10","text":"t (default 60 min, editable in the card). Only a process this plugin started is stopped — this is al"},{"id":"p5s11","text":"so the only thing that cleans up after a Harness that was killed. |\n| **Binary fetcher** | `node scr"},{"id":"p5s12","text":"ipts/install-binary.mjs` downloads and verifies the right release binary for your OS and CPU. |"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Nothing in DSH is patched: the plugin uses the documented `ctx.web.registerSearchProvider()`\n[该节后续省略"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"othing in DSH is patched: the plugin uses the documented `ctx.web.registerSearchProvider()`\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Do you need this plugin at all?"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"**If you use rustdsh (`rdsh`), let rustdsh handle search.** Since v0.15.0 it checks whether\nrustxng "},{"id":"p8s2","text":"/ `SEARXNG_URL` actually answers at start-up and, only when it does, passes\n`DSH_WEB_SEARCH_PROVIDER"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"=rdsh-rustxng` to the delegated DSH so the bundled\n`rdsh-web-search-searxng` provider takes `web_sea"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"rch` over (`web_search_bridge`, on by\ndefault)."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"| Your situation | Use |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| You start **DSH through rdsh** (`rdsh tui`, `rdsh web`, …"},{"id":"p9s2","text":") and want `web_search` to hit a local engine | **rustdsh's own bridge.** Nothing to configure; stop"},{"id":"p9s3","text":" it with `rdsh features off web_search_bridge` |\n| You start **`dsh` directly** (desktop app, system"},{"id":"p9s4","text":"d, …) and want `web_search` replaced | **This plugin.** rdsh only injects into the children it launc"},{"id":"p9s5","text":"hes, so a plain `dsh` boot is untouched |\n| You need **`web_fetch` to stop garbling** pages whose ch"},{"id":"p9s6","text":"arset is declared only in `<meta>` | **This plugin** (`webFetch.enabled`) — rustdsh's bridge is sear"},{"id":"p9s7","text":"ch only |\n| You want the agent to call RustXNG **as a tool** (`rustxng_search` / `rustxng_status`) |"},{"id":"p9s8","text":" **This plugin.** |\n| You want the binary **downloaded, started and idle-stopped** for you | **This "},{"id":"p9s9","text":"plugin** (`autoStart`); rustdsh never downloads anything on behalf of the bridge |\n| You use both an"},{"id":"p9s10","text":"d want **one instance for both** | Point rdsh at this plugin's instance: `RUSTXNG_URL=http://127.0.0"},{"id":"p9s11","text":"ne instance for both** | Point rdsh at this plugin's instance: `RUSTXNG_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8888` |"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"**Give search to exactly one of them.** With both, two providers are registered (`rustxng` and\n`rdsh"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"-rustxng`) and two sidecars can end up running. Letting rustdsh own it means turning this\nplugin's `"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"webSearch.enabled` off; letting this plugin own it means\n`rdsh features off web_search_bridge` (or `"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"RDSH_WEB_SEARCH_BRIDGE=0`)."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"**Delegating search to rustdsh does not change `web_fetch`.** Use this plugin's\n`webFetch.enabled` w"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"hen you want the fetch side replaced too. See\nIf you also use rdsh for sharing one instance and one "},{"id":"p11s3","text":" want the fetch side replaced too. See\nIf you also use rdsh for sharing one instance and one binary."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Requirements"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"- DeepSeek Harness `>= 0.2.0-rc.2 < 0.3.0` (host `tools`, `web` and `settings` services).\nVerified o"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"n **0.2.0-rc.2** and **0.2.1-rc.2**; see docs/PLATFORMS.md.\n- Node.js 20+ (the plugin uses the globa"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"l `fetch`)\n- A running RustXNG instance — see below"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## 1. Get RustXNG"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"**Easiest:** let the plugin fetch a release binary."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"The script picks the asset for your platform, verifies the published SHA-256, and prints\nthe start c"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"ipt picks the asset for your platform, verifies the published SHA-256, and prints\nthe start command."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"**Or** download it yourself from the\nreleases page:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"| Platform | Asset |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| Windows x64 | `rustxng-v<ver>-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.exe` |\n|"},{"id":"p19s2","text":" macOS arm64 | `rustxng-v<ver>-aarch64-apple-darwin` |\n| macOS x64 | `rustxng-v<ver>-x86_64-apple-da"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"rwin` |\n| Linux x64 (glibc) | `rustxng-v<ver>-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu` |\n| Linux x64 (musl) | `rust"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"xng-v<ver>-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl` |"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Start it:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"RustXNG serves its own search UI at <http://127.0.0.1:8888/>; this plugin does not replace\nthat page"},{"id":"p22s2","text":", it just consumes the same JSON API."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## 2. Install the plugin"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Installing from a checkout **links** the directory, so Node resolves the plugin's real path\n(`.../ds"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"h-rustxng`). The plugin copes with that: if `@deepseek-ai/schemastery` is not\nresolvable from there,"},{"id":"p25s3","text":" it loads the schema builder through the running Harness's own entry\npoint instead of silently dropp"},{"id":"p25s4","text":"chema builder through the running Harness's own entry\npoint instead of silently dropping the schema."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## 3. Turn it on"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Open **Plugins → RustXNG** and switch on *Use RustXNG for web_search*. Or set it in your\nprofile pat"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"ch (`~/.dsh/profiles/<profile>/cordis.patch.yml`):"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"From then on `web_search` is answered by RustXNG. The `enabled` and `autoSelect` switches\nand the in"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"stance URL are *volatile*: the settings card changes them live, and turning the\nfeature off hands `w"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"eb.searchProvider` back to whatever it was before."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"## Configuration"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"| Key | Default | Meaning |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
